    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0766" n="1556" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">OCB files, lot 61
                    D 385, “Prestige Project”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        European Affairs (Merchant) to the Under
                        Secretary of State (Smith)</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d231-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-19">April 19, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ambassador Dillon’s cable no. 3623 of March 31 from Paris<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d231-f2"/> confirms his conclusion of last summer that French
                    confidence in American leadership has continued to decline ever since the
                    beginning of 1953. The cable supplements Embassy despatches concerning the
                    rising tide of French concern over “McCarthyism” in the United States.</p>
                <p>The Secretary was disturbed by this cable and has indicated his interest in
                    referring it to Mr. Streibert and possibly the OCB to consider action which might be taken to correct the
                    impression which Ambassador Dillon reports has been created in France. You will
                    recall that the answers elicited last year by the Department’s “Eyes Only”
                    circular telegram no. 53 of June 23 were considered and noted by the NSC. Although the matter was not referred to the
                        OCB last year, I am informed that reference
                    of the present cable to the OCB would not call
                    for any further action on the part of the NSC.
                    Accordingly, it is recommended that you distribute to the members of the OCB at the next luncheon meeting copies of the
                    cable in question together with a covering memorandum. In addition to soliciting
                    the views of the members of the OCB as to
                    possible action, it is particularly recommended that Mr. Cutler’s views be
                    sought in view of past consideration of this subject by the NSC.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
